WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:30.310
- Hi everyone.

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:31.990
Sal Khan here from Khan Academy.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.930
Welcome to our daily livestream.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:37.240
For those of y'all who are
wondering what this is,

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.610
this is something we
started several months ago

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:41.340
as a way to keep us all connected

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.040
during times of social distancing

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.750
and just having interesting guests,

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:46.990
and have interesting conversations

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:49.540
and take your questions
and today like always,

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:53.080
I'll be taking your questions
on Facebook or on YouTube

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.540
and we have team members who can surface

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:57.244
what y'all are asking.

00:00:57.244 --> 00:00:59.730
We're going to do a last minute change

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:03.980
to today's livestream because
of all that's going on

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.427
in the world.

00:01:05.427 --> 00:01:08.100
We originally had one of
our great team members Marta

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.360
who's our VP of engineering
scheduled to join,

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:13.143
but given what's going on in the world,

00:01:13.143 --> 00:01:16.110
I thought it'd be better to save Marta

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:20.950
for a day where there
isn't all of this going on.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:25.800
And you know, I just wanna
give my two cents here

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.310
for whatever it's worth.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:32.310
A lot of times, I'm very
careful about saying

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.060
Khan Academy, and it's true.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.990
We are not a political organization.

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:40.060
We as an organization are
not left, we are not right,

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:43.500
we are just trying to
empower as many people

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.660
in the world to have
access to an education

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:48.750
and I think every now and then,

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:49.870
there's an issue that comes up

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.950
that frankly transcends politics

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.920
and I think that what's going on right now

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.180
with obviously what happened George Floyd,

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:00.800
but obviously that's just one
in a string of many incidents

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.500
where there is really
only one side to this

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:08.520
in that there's just
some basic human dignity

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.500
that isn't being given to folks.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:16.740
And you know, sometimes you
can rationalize that well,

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:19.740
the whole world there's going
to be things that happen

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:23.320
that are unfortunate but for
every one of these things

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.030
that captures folks' attention

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:29.270
that gets captured on
someone's cell phone,

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:32.610
you've got to imagine
that there's another 100

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:34.690
or another thousand that
don't get the attention

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:35.750
and don't get captured.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:38.500
And for every time something
horrible like this happens

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:42.690
that someone gets killed
or severely injured,

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:46.820
you have to imagine that
there's another thousand times

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:48.780
that it doesn't quite get that far,

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:53.660
but someone is humiliated or
someone is unjustly imprisoned

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:57.070
or just treated in an inhumane way.

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:58.510
And this is a real thing.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.790
This isn't just something
that happens on the news.

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:05.560
I remember when I was in business school,

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:09.630
this was back in 2003, one of
my classmates, Matt Turner,

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:11.290
I know he's written about this

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.410
so he probably wouldn't
mind me mentioning his name,

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:14.760
who's African American.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.400
He was section president,
he was an air force captain,

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.080
he had gone with me to MIT,

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:24.304
he was clearly at Harvard business school

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:27.960
and he was visiting some friends in Dallas

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:30.330
and while he was visiting,

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:31.860
he was just walking on the street

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:36.310
and all of the sudden, a
police helicopter and cops,

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:39.300
policemen started showing up with guns out

00:03:43.328 --> 00:03:46.250
and he was arrested for an hour

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:49.630
and frankly humiliated and it turns out

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:52.770
that the crime he was a suspect for

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:56.390
was committed by four white
men several miles away.

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:59.170
And that was the first time
that it was an aha in my mind

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:02.960
that this is not something
that is just an abstract thing

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.330
that happens in random parts of, you know,

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:07.520
places that are disconnected.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:08.740
They can happen to your friends,

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:10.210
they can happen to your family,

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:12.050
they can happen to people you care about

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:14.840
and if it happens to someone like Matt,

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:19.840
who is by any measure as kind of living

00:04:25.107 --> 00:04:27.653
the aspirational life that we,

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:31.113
or what we should aspire to I should say,

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:35.333
and has served for our military,

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:39.340
doing everything right on the.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.960
If he gets humiliated like that,

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.443
you can imagine what happens to folks

00:04:43.443 --> 00:04:48.443
that have a less of a
voice, less of a platform,

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:51.840
less representation.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:55.130
So this is a really huge thing.

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:57.720
All of us at Khan Academy,
we pride ourselves

00:04:59.673 --> 00:05:01.540
that we wanna help
level the playing field.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:03.150
We wanna make sure that everyone

00:05:05.265 --> 00:05:07.400
can tap into their potential.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.860
But if you don't have human dignity,

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:12.460
if you have to worry about your own safety

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:14.120
just because of the color of your skin,

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:15.930
because of the way you might look,

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:18.410
I think that just hampers
your ability to have

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:21.340
an openness to anything
else, to be able to engage

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:24.770
in your education or your
career or whatever else.

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:27.640
So anyway, you know, I
wish there were things

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:30.410
that I knew of that I
could take more action

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:32.650
other than just speaking out about it.

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:34.650
This transcends politics.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:36.950
The only thing that I
can right now imagine

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:38.260
that is going to make a difference

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:40.830
is for there to be real accountability.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:45.830
I think it's hard for anyone to imagine

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:48.750
a situation where this
shouldn't be held accountable

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:50.820
and you know, the whole theory of justice

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:52.640
is you might not capture every crime

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:55.650
or you might not be able to
hold everyone accountable,

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:58.920
but if there's at least
examples where people who

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.210
clearly did wrong are held accountable,

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:05.520
it can help create pause and keep others

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.260
from doing things in the future.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:09.200
And obviously it shouldn't just be about

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.740
the people who directly committed it,

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:13.840
it should be the people
who also kind of let

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:17.323
some of this stuff go
by for many many years.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:21.810
So anyway, I don't wanna pretend

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:26.600
that I'm a major actor in this,

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:29.560
but I did just wanna say
that this is something

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:32.020
that has unfortunately
it seems like we hear

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:35.800
stories about this every
three, four, five, six months

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:38.350
and they're disappointing,

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:41.230
but they just keep building on each other

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:43.560
and they're very very unfortunate

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:46.960
and just breaks your heart to see it

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:48.160
and it breaks your heart to think about

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:51.360
how many other situations
there might be like this

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:53.090
in the US and frankly around the world

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:57.890
where there's people in
groups who for whatever reason

00:06:57.890 --> 00:06:59.540
don't have as much voice

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:04.540
and people who have more power
sometimes abuse that power.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:07.724
And I wanna make it very clear,

00:07:07.724 --> 00:07:12.570
there's many great wonderful
people in law enforcement.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:16.070
I believe that the bulk
of people who desire

00:07:16.070 --> 00:07:18.020
to go into law enforcement wanna do it

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:19.510
because they wanna protect society,

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:23.803
they wanna uphold the values
that we all believe in.

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:29.740
But there is I think more
than just a few bad apples

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:33.430
in that for sure in any field,

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.480
there might be people who get into wrong,

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:39.880
for the wrong reason, but
they should not be allowed

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:42.300
to act on it, especially when
they have the public's trust,

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:43.850
especially when they are armed,

00:07:44.769 --> 00:07:45.810
especially when they can arrest folks

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:50.810
and physically manipulate, impact folks.

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:54.970
You have to have just a much much higher

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:57.887
standard of conduct and
a much higher standard

00:07:57.887 --> 00:08:02.490
of what it means to hold
other people accountable

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:04.940
and not allow this type of thing to go on.

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:07.570
So anyway, I'll get off on my soap box.

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:09.343
This is a bother.

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:14.170
I'm fortunate, I haven't
directly experienced this

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:17.560
in my life but obviously
folks close to me have

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:19.450
and when you see things like this,

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:21.403
it really disturbs you.

00:08:23.381 --> 00:08:27.600
But anyway, I'm happy to
look at questions, comments.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:31.130
This is really just kind of
an open minded discussion.

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:34.483
I'd love ideas if folks might have.

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:37.313
Let's see.

00:08:39.055 --> 00:08:41.345
A few folks are commenting
about my hair cut.

00:08:41.345 --> 00:08:42.363
Thank you.

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:45.420
I mean, on a lighter note,

00:08:46.406 --> 00:08:48.589
report about the hair cut situation is

00:08:48.589 --> 00:08:51.060
I was so excited about the SpaceX launch

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:54.050
which I guess was a silver
lining from the weekend

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:56.570
that my wife wanted to give me a hair cut

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:57.860
and I was in such a hurry

00:08:57.860 --> 00:09:00.130
I just took the clipper
from here and I did this.

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:03.480
But anyway, thanks for that comment.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:04.780
I have mixed feelings about it,

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:07.850
but that was a highlight of the weekend

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:11.240
to see kind of what I think is
some of the best of humanity

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:12.580
when we work together,

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:14.580
the cool things that we can do together.

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:17.530
And I hope that I can on the livestream

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:20.280
bring some folks from
SpaceX at some point or NASA

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:22.590
to talk about that, but you know,

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:25.070
it's sad that the same society that can do

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:28.770
incredible things like
that on the same level,

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:30.670
we can't give basic human dignity

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:33.683
to large chunks of our population.

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:37.200
Let's see, other, there's comments.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:42.200
I mean, there's a lot of good questions

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:46.250
and I'll just say, it just feels.

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:49.390
Normally I like answering
pretty much any question

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:52.020
that comes and some of
these are very flattering

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:55.770
to Khan Academy or to
me, but it just feels

00:09:55.770 --> 00:09:59.673
a little bit beside the point right now.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:04.390
And look, this crisis or
whatever we're going through

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:07.000
and obviously it's
layered on top of at least

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.700
one other large crisis,
it's not going to end today,

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:11.250
it's not going to end tomorrow,

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:17.063
but it is, this might be the thing

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:22.520
that finally makes this a major issue

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:25.430
that doesn't just get talked about

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:28.520
when there's another cell phone footage

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:31.620
of someone being abused or mistreated

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:36.500
or in this case killed for no other reason

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:39.580
than being in the wrong
place in the wrong time

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:40.933
with the wrong person.

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:45.250
But unfortunately we see a
little bit too much about that.

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:49.160
You know, this is a question
from Facebook related

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:51.190
to what we're seeing.

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:54.580
Mamta Bhattacharya, as an educator,

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:56.880
where should I start teaching
my students about racism?

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:01.128
You know, I don't wanna pretend
like I'm an expert at this,

00:11:01.128 --> 00:11:04.600
so I can't really give
a lot of advice on it.

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.830
I would love advice
actually from other folks

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:11.830
on what, you know, if there's
ways that Khan Academy

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:16.333
or folks like us could
help, we'd love to know.

00:11:17.377 --> 00:11:19.060
But I do have a general view that

00:11:20.177 --> 00:11:23.700
the more exposure you have to folks

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:27.380
that are not like yourself
and the more appreciation

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:30.720
that children have or
people of all ages have

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:34.010
that frankly everyone on the planet

00:11:34.010 --> 00:11:38.440
is pretty much just
normal people trying to

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:41.400
get on with their lives
and have basic health,

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:43.860
basic safety, basic education,

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:45.810
trying to do right by their children

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:49.703
and I've just pretty much
described almost everyone,

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:53.500
then hopefully we see a world where

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:57.403
some of this doesn't happen as much.

00:11:58.519 --> 00:12:03.519
I'm someone who prides myself
in being able to empathize

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:05.900
and seeing both sides of an issue

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:08.020
or all three sides of an issue,

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:12.300
but I genuinely have
trouble getting in the minds

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:17.300
of folks who harbor the
degree of hate or anger,

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:24.773
irrational with no other, you know,

00:12:28.876 --> 00:12:31.603
to be able to do these types of things.

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:37.500
There's no, there's been incidents before

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:40.240
that have been also atrocious,

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:44.640
but there's maybe there was fear,

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:46.110
maybe there was this or that,

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:49.880
but this is a situation
where you even if you're

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:52.390
grasping for straws, there's
no straws to grasp on

00:12:53.363 --> 00:12:56.650
and all you can think of is
that it's pure hate, pure anger

00:12:56.650 --> 00:13:00.257
and it's hard to understand that, frankly.

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:04.403
But yeah.

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:08.680
Let's see, from Facebook, I
wish I could be more helpful.

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:13.020
Deena Newman, we talked
with our kids about

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:15.240
having conversations with
people we are uncomfortable with

00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:16.700
and ask questions and
hear stories to change

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:18.420
the narratives we already
have in our heads.

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:19.940
Great, so there you go.

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:22.330
To Mamta's question, Deena
has kind of answered it,

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:26.277
which is we have to be
comfortable in our discomfort

00:13:26.277 --> 00:13:31.277
and that might be people
that we've stereotyped

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:34.140
in one way or the other
and it goes both ways.

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:35.590
I think we're in a time where

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:41.984
clearly a lot of African American folks

00:13:41.984 --> 00:13:45.810
or minority folks might get stereotyped

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:49.210
and are treated unfairly
and you know there's,

00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:53.940
this is a time where a
lot of very good people

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:56.240
who work in government or law enforcement

00:13:56.240 --> 00:14:00.070
are also probably themselves
shaking their heads

00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:00.903
and saying.

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:05.190
They're probably less
worried about themselves

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:06.780
and saying like, this is so unfortunate

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.550
that this is happening.

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:10.580
Because I mean, it's just so many layers.

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:12.560
Obviously the very act that it happens

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:14.807
and then there's the layer of

00:14:14.807 --> 00:14:18.800
it just breaks down trust

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:20.250
and sometimes it might become harder

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.110
to have those conversations
that you're referring to

00:14:23.110 --> 00:14:25.350
where folks can talk to people

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:29.060
who they might be initially
uncomfortable with

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:31.400
or who might feel like they
have a different life story

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:32.700
or life path than themselves.

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:36.250
So if there is a silver lining,

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:39.430
it's that this is kind of the straw

00:14:39.430 --> 00:14:41.580
that breaks the camels back.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:43.040
Real accountability's going to happen.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:44.590
It's not just in Minneapolis,

00:14:44.590 --> 00:14:46.640
but it's systematic real accountability

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:51.280
and I hope that the
energy just gets channeled

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:53.940
to more of these conversations

00:14:53.940 --> 00:14:54.870
that you're talking about.

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:57.210
I think the protests
are an important part.

00:14:57.210 --> 00:14:59.140
Obviously the peaceful protests are a very

00:14:59.140 --> 00:14:59.980
